 This checklist is normative release procedure. `GOVERNANCE.md` defines who may
 approve changes; CI enforces the mechanically verifiable items.
 
+Checking a box records evidence for the exact candidate commit; the prose or a
+local working tree is not evidence by itself. Unmet items remain unchecked.
+
+## Protocol 1.0.0-rc.4
+
+- [ ] `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, the generated
+  `conformance/v1/manifest.json`, and
+  `schemas/v1/conformance-claim-v2.schema.json` all identify
+  `1.0.0-rc.4`; claim v1 and its generated cases remain frozen at rc.3.
+- [ ] `decisions/0004-compile-only-build-drivers.md` is present and the
+  compatibility and security notes cover schema 6, `go-v1`, context
+  exclusion, receipts, marker v2, protected cache reuse, compiler-input risk,
+  dry-run, and transactional publication.
+- [ ] On the exact candidate checkout, `make validate` passes and verifies the
+  closed schema, schema-case, vector, fixture, expected-artifact, link, and
+  manifest-hash inventories.
+- [ ] Two independent `make regenerate` runs produce byte-identical
+  `conformance/v1` output, and `make regenerate-check` passes without a diff.
+- [ ] A schema-valid conformance claim v2 names the exact SHA-256 identity of
+  the generated rc.4 suite manifest, truthful implementation name and version,
+  claimed classes and operating systems, timestamp, and only `result: "pass"`.
+  Its supporting evidence is tied separately to the immutable implementation
+  commit. A claim v1 or rc.3 suite digest is not rc.4 evidence.
+- [ ] Every claimed manager commit consumes the exact released rc.4 suite from
+  `CURATOR_CONFORMANCE_ROOT` with no skipped, filtered, substituted, xfailed,
+  or implementation-private golden cases, including the real `go-v1` fixture,
+  every admitted Go release family, and Linux, macOS, and Windows evidence as
+  claimed.
+- [ ] Curator and the independent Python manager demonstrate interoperable
+  schema 6 reads, marker-v2 and receipt-v1 handling, context exclusion,
+  build/cache identities, compiler-free dry-run outcomes, transaction and
+  rollback behavior, repair, GC, and command launch behavior against the same
+  suite.
+- [ ] Only after those implementation commits and their required CI exist,
+  `.github/workflows/implementations.yml` pins their full immutable commit IDs;
+  this specification candidate does not infer support from a branch, mutable
+  tag, local run, or unreleased manager version.
+- [ ] Required independent security and interoperability evidence has no open
+  critical or high finding and identifies the exact reviewed candidate.
+- [ ] Candidate tag, signatures, checksums, archives, and provenance
+  attestations exist and verify before any release record claims them.
+
+Run the candidate gate only from the clean, exact candidate checkout:
+
+```text
+make release-check VERSION=1.0.0-rc.4
+```
+
+When a real claim-v2 file and its supporting implementation evidence exist,
+validate that claim against the same checkout with:
+
+```text
+python tools/release_gate.py --version 1.0.0-rc.4 --commit HEAD --claim <claim-v2.json>
+```
